<li class="comment even depth-3 parent highlander-comment" id="comment-95427">
	<div id="div-comment-95427">
	<div class="comment-author vcard">
		<img alt="" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546im_/https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/36f87527b3927a8931b393118a45d9dd?s=48&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=PG" class="avatar avatar-48" height="48" width="48"/>		<cite class="fn">Sarah Rose</cite> <span class="says">Says:</span>	</div>
		<br/>

	<small class="comment-meta commentmetadata"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546/https://abortion.ws/2013/09/04/late-term-abortion-bans-the-pros-and-cons/#comment-95427" title="">
	September 5, 2013 at 7:26 pm</a> </small>

	<p>No I for one would not budge an inch, once you give and inch they will want a foot and then a yard and then they won&#8217;t stop&#8230;</p>
<p id="comment-like-95427" data-liked="comment-not-liked" class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546/https://abortion.ws/2013/09/04/late-term-abortion-bans-the-pros-and-cons/?like_comment=95427&amp;_wpnonce=5bf62f6ba9" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="2048420"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-95427" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
<div class="pd-rating" id="pd_rating_holder_1235304_comm_95427"></div>
	<div class="reply">
		<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546/https://abortion.ws/2013/09/04/late-term-abortion-bans-the-pros-and-cons/?replytocom=95427#respond" onclick="return addComment.moveForm( &quot;div-comment-95427&quot;, &quot;95427&quot;, &quot;respond&quot;, &quot;3653&quot; )" aria-label="Reply to Sarah Rose">Reply</a>	</div>
	</div>
<ol class="children">
<li class="comment odd alt depth-4 parent highlander-comment" id="comment-95548">
	<div id="div-comment-95548">
	<div class="comment-author vcard">
		<img alt="" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546im_/https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/ad193117dce1efeca8b01e1acd012ef7?s=48&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=PG" class="avatar avatar-48" height="48" width="48"/>		<cite class="fn"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546/http://thesitethatdaresnotspeakitsname/" rel="external nofollow" class="url">RESPONSIBLE Right to Life/chuck/charles/aborticentrism</a></cite> <span class="says">Says:</span>	</div>
		<br/>

	<small class="comment-meta commentmetadata"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160909023546/https://abortion.ws/2013/09/04/late-term-abortion-bans-the-pros-and-cons/#comment-95548" title="">
	September 7, 2013 at 8:32 am</a> </small>

	<p>Sarah Rose, what about the bigger picture, namely, what happens after a child is born?  Are you ready to take care of the next child you insist be born?</p>
<p>Unfortunately, calmed1&#8217;s excellent monograph has no effect on people like you, because it comes from a rational basis.  Your &#8220;give them an inch&#8221; argument is typical of the ingrained sense of persecution the so-called &#8220;pro-lifers&#8221; bear.  Why do they revel in a mild form of paranoia rather than consider the full spectrum of life and fight for responsibility toward actual children?</p>
<p>There is a huge chasm between their professed concern for &#8220;human life&#8221; and their actual care for it, which indicates an underlying emotional problem.</p>
<p>This hypothesis is borne out by the fact that you, indeed, are not raising a child you don&#8217;t want to.</p>
