    		When a pregnant women feels a kick in her belly, she doesn't say "Oh, the fetus kicked" or "Oh, the mass of
    		cells that hasn't become a person kicked", she says "The <i eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:40px;wocalc:40px;hcalc:19px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[1]/a/li[1]/i;pagepos:117;cwidth:40;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:40px;wocalc:40px;hcalc:19;rend_px_area:0;minimum_paddings:0px 0px 0px 0px;rcnt:5;ez_min_text_wdth:38;req_px_area:1664;obj_px_area:0;req_px_height:20.8;req_margin_and_padding:0;req_ns_height:;vertical_margin:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;">baby</i> kicked."  Yes, after conception you have
    		a real human being waiting to enter the world. Why should taking someone's life when they're in the womb be any
    		different than taking their life when they're a baby in the crib? Pro-choice advocates claim this isn't a real
    		baby only to justify their wrong acts in their own minds. Even if you don't believe abortion is murder, it still
    		demeans the value of human life, since women can so callously stomp out a living being simply because
            they're inconvenienced.<br><br>

    		<b eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:1px;wocalc:1px;hcalc:0px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;font-weight:bold;nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[1]/a/li[1]/b[2];pagepos:119;cwidth:1;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:1px;wocalc:1px;hcalc:0;rend_px_area:0;minimum_paddings:0px 0px 0px 0px;rcnt:5;ez_min_text_wdth:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;"></b>
</li>
