              experience along with, in some cases, the father of the child.</b>
    		Many women who have abortion in their younger years end up living the rest of their lives in perpetual guilt.
    		Even if that women doesn't consider it murder at the time, that may change as she matures. Even Jane Roe (not
    		her real name), the original woman behind the famous court decision, has completely changed her mind on abortion.
    		She filed a petition to have the decision overturned to help relieve the guilt of
            hundreds of thousands of needless
    		deaths she blames on herself. Also, let's not forget that there are <i eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:30px;wocalc:30px;hcalc:19px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[1]/a/li[4]/i;pagepos:131;cwidth:30;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:30px;wocalc:30px;hcalc:19;rend_px_area:0;minimum_paddings:0px 0px 0px 0px;rcnt:5;ez_min_text_wdth:28;req_px_area:1248;obj_px_area:0;req_px_height:20.8;req_margin_and_padding:0;req_ns_height:;vertical_margin:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;">two</i>
            parents of every aborted child. The father may feel just as guilty.
            The father may even want the child, but he has no choice if the
            mother chooses abortion.<br><br>

