<b eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:94px;wocalc:94px;hcalc:140px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;font-weight:bold;nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[1]/li[2]/b[1];pagepos:154;cwidth:94;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:94px;wocalc:94px;hcalc:140;rend_px_area:0;minimum_paddings:0px 0px 0px 0px;rcnt:3;ez_min_text_wdth:94;req_px_area:13686.4;obj_px_area:0;req_px_height:20.8;req_margin_and_padding:0;req_ns_height:;vertical_margin:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;">Abortion eliminates legal rights of the unborn child.</b>
          The documents of our founding fathers state that we are all entitled to life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness.  By legalizing
          abortion, we take those rights away from a future American citizen.  Just because the babies can't speak for themselves
          doesn't mean they have no rights.  If a 1-month old is murdered, it that really different than abortion as far as protecting
          an American's life?  If a person shoots and kills a pregnant woman, shouldn't the punishment be more severe?  If you
          legalize abortion, it would tell the courts there is no difference.
