    				</b></a><b eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:162px;wocalc:162px;hcalc:40px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;font-weight:bold;nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[2]/li[1]/b[1];pagepos:194;cwidth:162;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:162px;wocalc:162px;hcalc:40;rend_px_area:0;minimum_paddings:0px 0px 0px 0px;rcnt:4;ez_min_text_wdth:134;req_px_area:9141.6;obj_px_area:0;req_px_height:20.8;req_margin_and_padding:0;req_ns_height:;vertical_margin:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161018165433/http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pregnancy#Complications" target="_blank" eza="cwidth:0px;;cheight:0px;;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:126px;wocalc:126px;hcalc:20px;rend_px_area:0;" cwidth="0" style="background-color:transparent;background-size:auto;color:rgb(0, 0, 238);nodepath:/html/body/div[5]/ol[2]/li[1]/b[1]/a;pagepos:195;cwidth:126;cheight:0px;wcalc_source:child;wcalc:126px;wocalc:126px;hcalc:20;rend_px_area:0;rcnt:2;ez_min_text_wdth:126;req_px_area:5241.6;obj_px_area:0;req_px_height:20.8;req_margin_and_padding:0;req_ns_height:;vertical_margin:0;margin-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-for-scale:0px 0px 0px 0px;">complications</a> can develop.</b> 
    		Any woman who has ever been pregnant will tell you that is not always very pleasant.  Weight gain, edema, back pain,
    		morning sickness, and constipation are among the common complaints.  After delivery, postpartum depression &amp; psychosis,
    		stretch marks, varicose veins, and other problems sometimes follow the woman.  And of course, during delivery, a number
    		of complications can develop that could cause permanent harm or kill the mother.  
