        </div><!-- close story-meta -->
    </header>


    <div class="story-body-supplemental">
    <div class="story-body story-body-1">
        <figure class="promo media video lede layout-large-horizontal " data-videoid="100000004686970" data-media-action="modal" data-autoplay="false" data-embedded="false" data-adsensitivity="" data-live="false" aria-label="media" role="group">
        <span class="visually-hidden">Video</span>



    <figcaption class="caption">
        <h4 class="headline">Voices From Abortion Bill Protests</h4>

        <div class="caption-video">
            <div class="summary-credit">
                <p class="summary">A proposal to ban abortions in Poland, even in cases of rape and when a woman\xe2\x80\x99s life is in danger, sparked so-called Black Monday rallies in several European cities.</p>
                <span class="credit video-credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">
                    By NATALIA V. OSIPOVA on                                                                <span class="visually-hidden">Publish Date </span>October 3, 2016.
                                    </span>
                <span class="credit photo-credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">
                    Photo by Radek Pietruszka/European Pressphoto Agency.
                </span>
                                    <a class="video-link" href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000004686970/voices-from-abortion-ban-protests.html?action=click&amp;contentCollection=world&amp;module=lede&amp;region=caption&amp;pgtype=article">Watch in Times Video &#187;</a>
                            </div>

            <div class="sharetools-video-container">
                                <div id="sharetools-video-tools-100000004686970" class="sharetools sharetools-video-tools">
                    <ul>
                        <li class="sharetool embed-sharetool">
                            <a href="javascript:;" data-share="embed" data-modal-title="">
                                <i class="icon sprite-icon"></i>
                                <span class="sharetool-text ">embed</span>
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                                <div id="sharetools-video-inline-100000004686970" class="sharetools sharetools-video-inline" data-shares="facebook|,twitter|" data-url="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254oe_/http://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000004686970/voices-from-abortion-ban-protests.html?action=click&amp;contentCollection=world&amp;module=lede&amp;region=caption&amp;pgtype=article" data-title="Voices From Abortion Bill Protests" data-description="A proposal to ban abortions in Poland, even in cases of rape and when a woman\xe2\x80\x99s life is in danger, sparked so-called Black Monday rallies in several European cities." data-content-type="video">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </figcaption>
</figure>
<p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="271" data-total-count="271">WARSAW \xe2\x80\x94 Despite pouring rain and a chill in the air, Anna Pietruszka-Drozdz, together with as many as 24,000 other Polish women and men, skipped work on Monday and instead came to Castle Square in Warsaw, dressed in black, to protest a sweeping new anti-abortion bill.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="298" data-total-count="569">\xe2\x80\x9cA complete and total abortion ban? This is beyond my wildest nightmares,\xe2\x80\x9d said Ms. Pietruszka-Drozdz, 37, a mother of two. \xe2\x80\x9cWomen don\xe2\x80\x99t have abortions because they are promiscuous and it\xe2\x80\x99s convenient. They do it because they need to, and it\xe2\x80\x99s often the most traumatic decision ever.\xe2\x80\x9d</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="375" data-total-count="944">On Black Monday, as it was called, huge protests against the new legislation swept through <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1WbI1BWQu0MGlv88G_VJi11OGzhU">90 Polish cities</a>. The Warsaw mayor\xe2\x80\x99s office said 24,000 Poles took to the streets of the capital, waving black flags to draw international attention to the proposed restrictions. On the event\xe2\x80\x99s <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://www.facebook.com/events/1659773451018196/">Facebook page</a>, organizers said the protest drew up to 116,000 participants nationwide.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="235" data-total-count="1179"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://www.nytimes.com/topic/destination/poland">Poland</a>\xe2\x80\x99s existing abortion law is already one of the most restrictive in Europe. Abortion is permitted in only three cases: a severe fetal anomaly, a threat to the mother\xe2\x80\x99s health and life, or a pregnancy from rape or sexual abuse.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="214" data-total-count="1393">Under the <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://www.ordoiuris.pl/pliki/dokumenty/stop_aborcji_2016.pdf">proposed legislation</a>, written by an organization called <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://stopaborcji.pl/author/mariusz_dzierzawski/">Stop Abortion</a>, all abortions would be criminalized. Women, doctors and anyone who assisted with the procedure could face up to five years in prison.</p><div id="story-ad-1" class="story-ad ad ad-placeholder nocontent robots-nocontent">
    <div class="accessibility-ad-header visually-hidden">
    <p>Advertisement</p>
</div>
<a class="visually-hidden skip-to-text-link" href="#story-continues-1">Continue reading the main story</a>
</div>
<p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="267" data-total-count="1660" id="story-continues-1">\xe2\x80\x9cThis is a barbarian proposal that will move <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://topics.nytimes.com/top/news/international/countriesandterritories/poland/index.html?inline=nyt-geo" title="More news and information about Poland." class="meta-loc">Poland</a> back to medieval times,\xe2\x80\x9d Barbara Nowacka, the leader of a liberal initiative, <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://www.ratujmykobiety.pl/">Save Women</a>, said in a telephone interview. \xe2\x80\x9cThe worst thing is that this barbarity finds approval in the eyes of those in power.\xe2\x80\x9d</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="190" data-total-count="1850">Black Monday was the high point of protests that began two weeks ago. On social media, tens of thousands of Poles have posted <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://www.facebook.com/search/top/?q=%23blackprotest">pictures of themselves</a> wearing black and staging demonstrations.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="102" data-total-count="1952">Foreign Minister Witold Waszczykowski dismissed the protesters, saying, \xe2\x80\x9cLet them have their fun.\xe2\x80\x9d</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="222" data-total-count="2174">\xe2\x80\x9cThere is no such problem as a threat to women\xe2\x80\x99s rights,\xe2\x80\x9d he said in an interview with a private radio station, <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://www.rmf.fm/">RMF-FM</a>. \xe2\x80\x9cIf someone thinks that there are no greater concerns in Poland at the moment, let them be.\xe2\x80\x9d</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="257" data-total-count="2431">The protests have won the approval of numerous Polish employers, including restaurant owners, museum and gallery directors, the deans of several universities and mayors of a couple of large cities, all of whom allowed their female workers to take a day off.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="511" data-total-count="2942">The protest idea was inspired by the story of Icelandic women who paralyzed their country in 1975 <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/http://timesmachine.nytimes.com/timesmachine/1975/10/25/76619426.html?pageNumber=34">by not going to work</a>, and skipping housework and child-rearing tasks, to protest unfair employment practices and wage discrepancies. The women who participated in those protests sent the women in Poland a video <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z2bGy2DuUZ0">message of solidarity</a>, encouraging them to stand up for themselves and telling them in Polish, \xe2\x80\x9cJestesmy z wami\xe2\x80\x9d (\xe2\x80\x9cwe are with you\xe2\x80\x9d). On Facebook, Kenyan women also sent a <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://www.facebook.com/FundacjaRazemPamoja/videos/1163061223760094/">message of solidarity</a>.</p><p class="story-body-text story-content" data-para-count="130" data-total-count="3072">The solidarity protests were also staged in other European cities, including <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://twitter.com/kaodro/status/782903145236226049">Berlin</a>, <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20161007020254/https://twitter.com/CFerKic/status/782887240544509952">Brussels</a>, London, Paris and Barcelona, Spain.</p><div class="newsletter-signup  dropzone-11 ab-test-newsletter-module hidden" id="newsletter-promo" data-newsletter-productcode="TH">
    <h2 class="headline">Today&rsquo;s Headlines</h2>
